    "why": "No push-up yet: the push-up ladder starts at level 1 and, with no bench for a dumbbell press, incline push-ups carry the pressing; floor push-ups wait. A hard sit-to-stand gives box squats, a back that rounds in the hinge gives glute bridges instead of Romanian deadlifts, an 8 s hang (and no bar) leaves the pull-up ladder at level 1, a 20 s plank starts the core ladder at dead bugs, and balance under 30 s on one side keeps split squats with both feet down and adds a balance hold to the warm-up. Go, ramped keeps the first mesocycle at RIR 3; confidence 6 and \"I stop for a while\" lead the pre-mortem."
